messages:
lara: quick heads-up, opened PR to adjust the Console observability docs—adding a tiny tracing hook example + fixing a broken cost-link. PR: github.com/redwood/docs/pull/910

ben: pinging to review the SDK snippet. are you targeting Node only?

lara: yes node minimal example using @redwood/inference-sdk. main issue: span names in the snippet don't match Console grouping, plus one link goes 404 on preview.

miriam: paste the snippet so we can tweak it quickly

lara: ```js
const {Tracer} = require('@redwood/inference-sdk');
const tracer = new Tracer({service: 'observability-demo'});
app.post('/api/serve', async (req, res) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan('handler');
  await runtime.request(req.body);
  span.end();
  res.sendStatus(200);
});
```

ben: Console groups by route and model. Change startSpan to `route:${req.path}` and add `span.setTag('model', modelId)` so dashboards pick it up.

lara: good call. I'll update snippet. also the cost/latency guide uses "p99 latency" text only  should include PromQL example like `quantile(0.99, rate(latency_seconds[5m]))`.

miriam: add a 1-line migration note: "If migrating from startSpan('handler'), update to the route pattern and set the model tag to keep existing dashboard rows." Also mention private deployments: ensure OTLP endpoint is reachable from VPC.

lara: adding those. i found the broken link: /console/dashboards/cost-breakdown -> new slug /console/observability/cost-breakdown. will patch.

deploy-bot: docs preview build queued for pull/910 (https://ci.redwood.dev/builds/61234).

lara: pushed changes, requesting review.

docs-bot: Preview updated: https://preview.docs.redwood.dev/pull/910 (checks running).

ben: quick grammar nit: code block had missing backticks around modelId in the comment. fixed in a tiny commit.

miriam: preview looks good, route labels show up in trace table and cost widget renders. ready to merge after CI.

lara: merged. thanks everyone. closing thread. :tada:
